mac80211: minstrel_ht: add support for 160 MHz bandwidth in the 5 GHz band

Add VHT rate groups for 160 MHz (1-4 spatial streams, long and short
guard interval), so that stations operating at 160 MHz can use the full
channel width.

Many chips cannot send as many streams at 160 MHz as at 80 MHz; MT7615
for example sends at most two. Add ieee80211_hw.vht160_max_nss for a
driver to declare that limit, and leave out 160 MHz groups with more
streams.

On an 80+80 channel these rates go out as 80+80 PPDUs, so use them only
with peers that advertise 80+80 support.

Also compute the expected throughput in 64 bits, as the 160 MHz rates can
overflow an int there.

